<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 92-day T-bill yields avg 3.706 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 92-day T-bill yields avg 3.706 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$3.0 billion of 92-day Government of Canada treasury bills due January 3, 1997 was 3.706 percent, down from 3.962 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 175-day T-bills due March 27, 1997 was 4.085 percent, down from 4.260 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due October 2, 1997 was 4.408 percent, down from 4.663 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$825 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.2 billion of C$5.8 billion of bills due Oct. 10.</p>
